<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 8 Lesson 8 multiplication fluency">
<h2>Multiplication Center Day — individual fluency and partner games</h2>
<p><strong>Mental Number Talk:</strong> 2 × 4 = 8; 5 × 4 = 20; 10 × 4 = 40; 17 × 4 = 68. Explain why 40 + 20 + 8 = 68.</p>
<p><strong>Card sort:</strong> With a partner, sort facts from 1 × 1 to 10 × 10 into <em>know right away</em>, <em>find quickly</em>, and <em>don't know yet</em>. Select <strong>five</strong> facts to rehearse and explain strategies, e.g. 9 × 8 = (10 × 8) − 8.</p>
<p><strong>Compare center:</strong> Two players split independent multiplication cards, reveal one each, and compare products. The greater product wins both; most cards at the end wins. Example: 12 × 9 &gt; 12 × 7 because their difference is 24.</p>
<p>Teacher checks authentic pair interactions and learners' reflections. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-8/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original 2021 teacher lesson</a>. Publisher card masters and restricted Cool-down are not claimed to be digitally reproduced.</p>
